Now I have a clear picture. The rendered surface is the page showing content (title, description, etc.) from Contentstack. The live preview feature means: when a content author edits content in Contentstack CMS, the rendered page should update to reflect those edits in real time.

The root cause is that `contentstack.Stack(stackOptions)` is called without `live_preview` config in the options, so the SDK never enters live-preview mode, `isLivePreviewEnabled()` returns false, and `onEntryChange` never fires.

Verification criteria must be observable on the rendered page:

1. When a content author modifies a field value in Contentstack's live preview mode, the rendered page displays the updated value without a full page reload.
2. When live preview is active, the rendered page reflects content changes within seconds of the author editing them in the CMS.
3. When the page is loaded outside of live preview (normal delivery), the page renders the published content values correctly.
4. When the live preview connection is unavailable, the page renders the last published content without displaying errors or blank content.

